      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While ibuprofen can help with pain and inflammation, it may not be the best choice for dizziness. For nausea and dizziness, consider taking an anti-nausea medication like meclizine (such as Bonine) or dimenhydrinate (like Dramamine) if you need to make a purchase or find it at the store before your shift. However, always consult with your supervisor and a doctor before taking any new medication, especially if you're not sure if it will interact with any other medications or cause any other side effects.",
